    "title": "Speaking and interaction practice",
    "subtitle": "Choosing what fits · 1",
    "context": "Use the selected vocabulary and constructions to compare quantity, suitability and price before making a purchase.",
    "steps": [
      {
        "id": "EX-CORE-U3-06-required-speaking-produce",
        "kind": "check",
        "title": "Explain the situation",
        "questions": [
          {
            "id": "EX-CORE-U3-06-required-speaking-draft",
            "kind": "production",
            "response": "spoken",
            "prompt": "Choosing what fits · 1: Explain the practical problem and your proposed response to an absent partner. State one constraint or condition and explain how it changes the plan.",
            "promptLanguage": "en",
            "context": "爸爸让我买两件大衣，一件白色，一件黑色。我去了商店，告诉卖衣服的人要什么。她听见两件，就先拿来两件白色的大衣。\n\n我说：“不是两件白色的。白色一件，黑色一件。”因为她刚才听错了，所以拿来了一件黑色的大衣。我把一件白色的和一件黑色的放在一起，请她看颜色对不对。\n\n我给爸爸打电话，再问是不是这样。他说对，让我看看大不大。我一件一件地看，发现黑色的比白色的大一点儿，又请她拿一件和白色的一样大的。\n\n回家以后，爸爸先看颜色，再看是不是一样大，两件都是他想买的。他问我是不是只说了两件，我说开始说了颜色，后来又问是不是一样大。\n\n这次我知道了，要买对东西，不能只看几件。颜色、大不大都要问明白。我把两件大衣放好，爸爸不用再去商店，也不用再打电话问。",
            "contextLanguage": "zh",
            "label": "Take your speaking turn",
            "resultDomain": "Self-reviewed speaking practice",
            "rubric": [
              {
                "id": "r1",
                "text": "My problem and proposed response follow the source."
              },
              {
                "id": "r2",
                "text": "I connected a real condition or constraint to the result."
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "sequential": true
      }
